selenium-webdriver-at-spi-screenshotter: capture an area, start without a
platform plugin

The helper ignored its x y width height arguments and always captured the
whole active output (CaptureActiveScreen). With a non-empty area it now calls
ScreenShot2.CaptureArea, so KWin renders and reads back only that part: on
llvmpipe a dock item costs 29 ms instead of 180 ms (debian-13) and 13 ms
instead of 52 ms (fedora-43). The image still goes through the same Qt
conversion and PNG writer; for a dock item, the dock surface and a screen
row the flattened area equals the same crop of a full capture (checked on
both targets). "0 0 0 0", what the webdriver passes,
still captures the active output. QCoreApplication replaces QGuiApplication:
talking D-Bus and encoding a QImage needs no Wayland connection.

